# Line-ending normalisation is on by default for anything Git decides is text,
# and it decides by sniffing the first few KB for NUL bytes. A ReportLab PDF is
# mostly ASCII up there, so Git classified docs/*.pdf as text and rewrote LF to
# CRLF on checkout — which shifts every byte offset in the PDF's xref table and
# hands anyone who clones the repo a damaged file. Verified: the documents grew
# by ~160 bytes on a fresh clone and readers reported a bad startxref pointer.
#
# Declaring the binary types explicitly is the fix. PNG and XLSX were already
# detected correctly, but they are listed so the next binary format added does
# not have to rediscover this.
* text=auto
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
# Large committed data — treat as text but never diff it in a review.
*.geojson  -diff
web/data/engine/*.json  -diff
backend/models/*.json   -diff
*.jp2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
